(about . "tests/fixtures/coverage-ladder-c0.my — WSM-CONSTITUTIONAL-COVERAGE-LADDER, first bounded slice: C0 (McCarthy-7 primitives: quote/atom/eq/car/cdr/cons/cond), my-lisp/oracle-tier evidence only. Joins tests/fixtures/dependency-classification.my's 'core' bucket (41 fixtures) with tests/fixtures/inventory.my's expected outcome and tests/fixtures/oracle-results.my's actual oracle outcome. cml/hosted/qemu/fpga columns are deliberately not-evaluated-here -- that evidence belongs to CML-CONSTITUTION-*, WSM-OS-CONSTITUTION-*, and FPGA-CONSTITUTION-* tasks in their own repos, not guessed here.")
(scope . "dependency-classification.my's 'core' bucket is broader than the strict McCarthy-7: it also covers other core special forms and Rust builtins (per that task's own note, two of its six buckets are hardcoded because they live in Rust with no self-hosted source to read). Each row's obligation-group says which kind of obligation it actually is: mccarthy-7-positive-semantics (G1/G2/G3/G5/G8-axiom fixtures -- the real McCarthy-7 semantic obligations), core-error-boundary (S2/S3-axiom fixtures -- error/arity/type/overflow contract obligations on core operations, part of the same McCarthy foundation per docs/language-core-axioms.md and docs/language-core.md's 'Invalid list operations produce explicit errors'), other-core-or-builtin (untagged fixtures the coarse dependency-classification bucket includes that are not strict McCarthy-7 obligations, e.g. princ/cond-truthiness fixtures without a G/S axiom tag -- listed honestly rather than silently folded into the McCarthy-7 count).")
(generated . "Not a script -- hand-assembled by direct join of the three existing generated artifacts (dependency-classification.my, inventory.my, oracle-results.my) via a one-off Python join script (not committed; the three source files are themselves the generated, re-derivable ground truth). A future pass could promote this join into a proper WSM script the way build-dependency-classification.my and oracle-batch.wsm already are, if C1-C7 slices make that worth doing.")
(summary . "41/41 fixtures PROVEN at the my-lisp/oracle tier: 0 not-proven, 0 missing-data, 0 divergence between oracle-results.my's actual outcome and inventory.my's expected outcome. 18 mccarthy-7-positive-semantics (axioms G1/G2/G3/G5/G8), 14 core-error-boundary (axioms S2/S3), 9 other-core-or-builtin (untagged). cml/hosted/qemu/fpga: not-evaluated-here for all 41, by design -- see scope above.")
